.TH HTTP_READ 3
.SH NAME
http_read \- read the body of a response as a buffer operation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "ssize_t http_read(fd_type " fd ", char* " buf ", size_t " len ", buffer* " b ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR http_read ()
has the shape of an operation of
.BR buffer (3),
so that the body of a response can be read with the buffer functions (also
through decompression filters, as buffer_lzma(3) does). The http structure is
.IR b->cookie
(or
.I fd
if there is no cookie). It reads from the socket into the input buffer, parses the headers
with
.BR http_read_internal (3)
while the status is HTTP_RECV_HEADER, and then returns body data.
.P
This belongs to the first reader of the module, written for
.BR buffer (3)
operations; it expects
.I h->stream
to be cleared. New code should use
.BR http_recv (3).
.SH RETURN VALUE
The number of bytes stored in buf, 0 at the end of the body or when there is nothing for now, -1 with errno set on an error.
.SH SEE ALSO
http_recv(3), http_read_internal(3), http_canread(3)
